{
  "id": "modes/sd/sum",
  "title": "SD: Sum of values (Σx)",
  "shortTitle": "Sum of values (Σx)",
  "parent": "modes/sd",
  "order": 2,
  "aliases": [
    "Σx",
    "sum x",
    "S-SUM 2",
    "total"
  ],
  "keywords": [
    "Σx",
    "sum",
    "S-SUM",
    "frequency"
  ],
  "formulas": [
    "Σx = Σ xi",
    "Σx = Σ (xi · fi)"
  ],
  "keySequence": [
    "SHIFT",
    "1",
    "2"
  ],
  "summary": "Sum of the x-values. With FreqOn each class is weighted by its frequency.",
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Σx is the running total of all observations. Every DT adds that value (times its frequency, if you used one)."
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "plain": "\\sum x = x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_n\n\\text{FreqOn: }\\sum x = \\sum x_i f_i"
    },
    {
      "type": "keys",
      "keys": [
        "SHIFT",
        "1",
        "2",
        "EXE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "lines",
      "items": [
        "Data: 2, 4, 6, 8 (four numbers)",
        "Sum = 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20",
        "Σx = 20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "items": [
        "MODE 4. If you were already in SD, SHIFT 9 → 1 (Stat) → EXE to clear the old list",
        "2 DT",
        "4 DT",
        "6 DT",
        "8 DT",
        "then AC",
        "SHIFT 1 → 2 EXE → Σx = 20"
      ],
      "title": "On the calculator"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Example with frequencies (FreqOn)"
    },
    {
      "type": "lines",
      "items": [
        "75 once, 80 twice, 85 four times",
        "Σx = 75×1 + 80×2 + 85×4",
        "Σx = 75 + 160 + 340 = 575"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "items": [
        "Confirm FreqOn in SETUP, then MODE 4",
        "75 DT",
        "80 DT DT",
        "85 ; 4 DT",
        "then AC",
        "SHIFT 1 → 2 EXE → Σx = 575"
      ],
      "title": "On the calculator"
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "text": "x̄ = Σx / n. If Σx looks wrong, a leftover Stat buffer or a frequency typed with FreqOff (Syntax ERROR / skipped) is the usual cause."
    }
  ],
  "related": [
    "modes/sd/n",
    "modes/sd/sumsq",
    "modes/sd/mean"
  ]
}
